course: dictionary
lesson: 5714
title: Reading about Viking longships
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A longship is a long, narrow wooden ship with oars and a square sail. The Vikings used longships for raiding, trading and exploring. When you meet a new word in a history book, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Viking longships were light and fast, with sails and oars» tells you what a longship was like.
explain: The clues help you build the meaning. «Their longships were light and fast and could sail up shallow rivers» shows the ship could go places that bigger ships could not. Ask yourself: what kind of ship would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the parts of a word too. Longship is made from long and ship, and together they give a clue: a ship that is long. You can use the clues in a sentence and the parts of the word together. If you are still stuck, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A longship is a long, narrow wooden ship with oars and a square sail.
fact: «Viking longship» is a phrase used when talking about these ships.
fact: The Vikings used longships for raiding, trading and exploring.
fact: Longships could sail across the sea and also up shallow rivers.
fact: Vikings in longships raided Lindisfarne in 793, and many longships had a carved dragon head at the front.
exercise: «Viking longships were light and fast, with sails and oars.» Which thing is a longship? | A huge stone castle on a hill | *A long, narrow wooden ship with oars and a square sail | A horse that pulls a cart | A small plane that flies over the sea
exercise: Mia says a longship could only sail on the open sea. What does the text say? | *It could sail across the sea and also up shallow rivers | It could only sail up very deep rivers | It could never leave the harbour | It could only fly over the water
exercise: «Their longships were light and fast and could sail up shallow rivers.» Which word tells you the ships could move quickly? | *fast | rivers | Vikings | light
test: What were Viking longships used for? | Building castles | *Raiding, trading and exploring | Growing crops on farms | Flying in the sky
test: «Their longships could sail up shallow rivers, so Vikings could appear far from home without warning.» Why could Vikings arrive without warning? | *Their ships could sail up shallow rivers and get close to places unseen | They flew over the land | They sent letters ahead to tell people | They always waited at home for visitors
exam: Which description best fits a longship and what it could do? | A small wooden raft used only on lakes | A tall stone tower built on the coast | A metal ship with engines that never used oars | *A long, narrow wooden ship with oars and a square sail, able to cross the sea and sail up shallow rivers
